afk: Anthropic multi-account ranking prefers the account whose shared 7d
window resets soonest, plus session-verified identity lookups and
pin-time rate-limit unblocking.

Motivation: Anthropic weekly windows recover on a fixed schedule, so
burning down the account whose 7d window resets soonest wastes the least
quota if it is exhausted. Display paths (status line) also need to name
the account a session is *verifiably* routed to, not the first stored
account the plain lookup falls back to before any getApiKey.

What must survive a rebase:
- `preferEarlierSecondaryReset?: boolean` on CredentialRankingStrategy
  (usage.ts) and the claude strategy opting in (usage/claude.ts).
- `secondaryResetAt` on UsageRankedCandidate, populated at BOTH ranking
  sites (api-key and oauth) via #resolveWindowResetAt, +Infinity when
  unknown, so unknown resets sort last.
- The comparator step sits after the hasPriorityBoost tie-break and
  BEFORE the short-window hot guard (and everything below it), with the
  60s tie tolerance (SECONDARY_RESET_TIE_TOLERANCE_MS) so near-identical
  schedules keep load-balancing.
- `provider` threaded into #orderUsageRankedCandidates and both compare
  helpers so the strategy flag can be resolved during ranking.
- `getOAuthAccountIdentity(provider, sessionId, { sessionStickyOnly })`:
  sticky-only lookups suppress the pre-attribution fallback to the first
  stored credential.
- A fresh manual pin clears reactive rate-limit blocks on the target so
  the next request actually tries it; a persisted-session restore
  (options.lastUsedAtMs) keeps existing blocks.

Rebase notes (17.2.14 -> 18.0.11): upstream added
`pinSessionOAuthAccount` (used by the /account command and the
credential-pin session-restore path), absorbing this patch's former
`pinSessionCredential` API. The pin part of this patch is now just the
block-clearing fold into that upstream method, gated to fresh manual
pins. Upstream also added the `usageMeasured` comparator step; the
soonest-reset preference still ranks above it.

